// The prologue's ship deck "Fehler" (docs/STORY.md, Prolog im Detail): one plane, 1 m a character, x east, y north.
// The first row of the grid is the north edge (y = 419), the last the south edge (y = 0); a character at column x of
// the row for y covers [x, x+1] x [y, y+1]. Read by import/Machines.Import/Planets/DeckParser.cs and tools/deck/deck.mjs.
// Legend: # wall (8 m)   . floor   v duct (crawl only)   ^ duct lip (raised mouth, crawl only)   g grate wall (blocks
// movement, shots and sight pass)   c high cover, 2 m (crates, consoles)   = catwalk (visual height only)
// h high stack, 8 m (crate towers, lockers, pipe banks, clamp gantries, lashed containers): a wall for movement, shots, sight
// A-Z a door or gate slot named in DOORS (an artefact while closed).
// Sections: DOORS letter name kind state | MARKERS name x y angle [tags] | PROPS name type x y angle id |
// ZONES name x0 y0 x1 y1 [tags] | LIGHTS name zone on|off|emergency | CAMS name x y z yaw pitch | RAILS name x y z ... |
// SLIDES name prop x0 y0 x1 y1 [tags] (a rail a prop slides along). A zone tagged variant=<name> cells=<c> is filled with c
// when the deck is read with that variant (off by default; deck B's short way is variant=short). Door kinds: door, blast,
// gate, vent, shutter (closes by itself, held in its frame). Door artefacts are tagged 1000 + 10 x their place in DOORS
// (the second leaf one more); props keep ids below 1000
// Angles in degrees, 0 east, 90 north. Room titles:
//   R2    Bucht 6 (Ike)
//   R1    Bucht 7 (L-7)
//   R3    Bucht 8 (Bob)
//   R0    Buchtengang
//   R4    Wartungsdeck A
//   WL    West link
//   EL    East link
//   R5    Lager
//   R7    Schaltraum
//   S     Service passage
//   R6    Wartungsdeck B
//   R8    Vorraum Rechnerkern
//   R9    Rechnerkern
//   R10   Hauptgang
//   R10a  Kaserne-Lift
//   P1    Parallelgang 1
//   P1s   Parallelgang 1, stub to the spine
//   P2    Parallelgang 2
//   K     Kabelgang
//   R12   Kreuzung
//   R13   Waffenkammer (Werkstatt)
//   R13a  Werkstattgang
//   R14   Reparaturnische
//   R15   Notgang
//   R15a  Notgang, mouth into the pod bay
//   R16   Pod-Bucht
//   A1    Leitstand
//   A2    Nische
//   ENi   E-Nische
//   R13n  Lastenrampe
//   R15b  Lastenlift
//   R17   Frachtraum
//   R18   Rohrgalerie
//   R19   Schachtsteg
//   R20   Kühlschlange (the escape's long way round the buried Notgang)
//
// Scaled 2x as a whole from the stage 5 deck (65a7b84) by tools/deck/scale.mjs with tools/deck/prolog-x2.plan, with
// extra way in five places (docs/story/deck/scale.md: why, the mapping of old points, the doors, rooms and the pod size).
// The Grunts' doors are 8 m, the Reapers' blast doors 12-16 m; the crawl ducts are 3 m wide (play test 2026-11-24: at 4 m a Grunt, 3.1 m wide, looked as if it would fit; L-7 is 2.7 m).
// The 2 on the DECK line is that scale: the sim's size classes need twice their room (Deck.GapScale, NavGrid). Grate windows
// into a duct reach the duct's kept band.

DECK prolog 630 420 2
GRID
